sheets.prompt:
Two images are attached. IMAGE 1 shows the game's five character HEADS (right-facing profile, all built on the same skull).
IMAGE 2 is an art-style reference (look at the tactical helmet and gear).

Generate a game-ready sheet of SEVEN separate HEADWEAR items that fit EXACTLY on the heads of IMAGE 1 (same scale: each head there is about
290 px from crown to chin), every item drawn alone in strict right-facing profile, as it would sit on that head, laid out as a grid of
2 rows x 4 columns with wide empty space around each:
Row 1: (1) a modern TACTICAL COMBAT HELMET (high-cut, with side rails, a front NVG mount plate and a few velcro panels), olive drab, hugging the
           skull, its rim sitting just above the ear and the brow;
       (2) a soft military BERET pulled to the right side, plain light grey (it will be colour-tinted in code), with a small badge;
       (3) a tied BANDANA headband wrapped around the forehead with two short tails at the back, plain light grey;
       (4) a BASEBALL CAP with the brim pointing RIGHT, plain light grey crown, dark brim underside.
Row 2: (5) a tactical radio HEADSET with an ear cup over the ear, a thin headband and a boom microphone pointing forward-right, dark grey;
       (6) a knitted BEANIE with a folded cuff, plain light grey;
       (7) a wide-brimmed BOONIE HAT, plain light grey, with a chin strap;
       (8) EMPTY cell.
Draw ONLY the headwear (no head, no face, no hair). Each item is hollow where the head would be, so it can be layered over the head.
Bold, clean, even dark outline (about 4 px), simple two-tone cel shading, light from the top-left, chunky shapes that stay readable when the
head is only 30 px tall in game.

Rules for the whole sheet:
- Fully transparent background. NO heads, NO faces, NO text, NO labels, NO glow, NO drop shadows, NO halos.
- Items never touch each other. Image size 1536x1024 (landscape).
